"""What a milestone is. One definition, used by the goal intake and by the coach, so they cannot drift apart."""
from __future__ import annotations

MILESTONE_RULES = """A milestone is ONE outcome with ONE deadline: a checkpoint that sits above the weekly plan. It is not a stretch of work and not a list.
- Never bundle outcomes into one milestone with "and", commas or colons. "Shortlist and system design basics: 15 employers, must-haves set, introduction, how to prepare, delivery framework read" is five milestones: "Shortlist of 15 employers ready", "Must-have list set", "System design introduction read", "How to prepare for system design read", "Delivery framework read".
- Name the finished state ("Resume sent to 10 recruiters"), not the activity ("Work on resume").
- Each milestone gets its own date, in the order they happen, none after the goal's deadline.
- Use as many milestones as the goal has distinct checkpoints, usually four to twelve. Do not merge them to keep the count low."""
